#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1073-A expect=skipped domain=TU
#note "Scope.Domains.Include: [TR] rejects the primary at the TU domain -> the rule never runs, skipped. TU is the sibling tumour domain and it legally carries ALL FOUR of the qualifiers TR prohibits (TULOC, TULAT, TUDIR, TUPORTOT); the skip pins that the corpus realises the sheet row's generic DOMAINS='ALL' as a per-domain prohibition, not a corpus-wide sweep."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TU class=FINDINGS label="Tumor Identification"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col TUSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TUTESTCD type=Char label="Tumor Identification Short Name"
col TULOC    type=Char label="Location of the Tumor"
col TULAT    type=Char label="Laterality"
col TUDIR    type=Char label="Directionality"
col TUPORTOT type=Char label="Portion or Totality"
---
S1 | TU | 001 | 1 | TUMIDENT | LIVER | LEFT | PROXIMAL | ENTIRE
---
